:answer-field/id #uuid "73f7dd8a-46cc-50f8-8f6c-5dc06aa45a32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490141}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3250f349-fbfe-56f8-96e2-52cb212003b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-102142" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7dad50d17444096c60b129131104209b8b7371d546f80d7b0c838baec1df8b4d.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-5x+6?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,5),B(1,2)$ and $C(2,-4).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x+6 \\\\ (5) & =-5(0)+6 \\\\ 5 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x+6 \\\\ (2) & =-5(1)+6 \\\\ 2 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x+6 \\\\ (-4) & =-5(2)+6 \\\\ -4 & =-4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4f3252-d422-5b2b-87b7-6916c51a12a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489550} {:answer/id #uuid "38679d57-742c-5817-a31c-101bf33ca332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489640} {:answer/id #uuid "685aeab1-eebd-534e-8e4a-d21630e148b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489763} {:answer/id #uuid "a111be60-4cf1-5eab-b12f-bf275dc291fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489871} {:answer/id #uuid "f9fd167a-76c2-572d-ac6f-8214ea48c14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490058}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489550} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e6c0ec-30d3-5bc5-89e9-08b3f00c0259" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "acf0d12e-cf58-5db7-b66f-2999c47f2d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71829" :question/problem "![](images/c3/c33968d9b5c86e39ba35c88a5f28bb8950178004c763a5c011633b9a060e98a8.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=4x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,-2)$, $B(0,1)$ and $C(1,6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4x+2 \\\\ (-2) & =4(-1)+2 \\\\ -2 & =-2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4x+2 \\\\ (1) & =4(0)+2 \\\\ 1 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,6)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4x+2 \\\\ (6) & =4(1)+2 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498666 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e65719-9423-5445-8fcf-aaf6c05d97d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498676} {:answer/id #uuid "643d71ec-95bc-5042-8b51-322a436c9046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498683} {:answer/id #uuid "80feb855-589a-53c3-bac3-61637b4af9e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498690} {:answer/id #uuid "e967faa4-e8a6-581c-a3cf-38284b6b90c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498712} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf14a96-818d-5db6-9c66-a0d3175bb6b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498714}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498676} :answer-field/id #uuid "fffeded8-fcf5-542f-a921-ded34513e23b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0f863f32-c463-5f07-9482-1c6f6e74c019" :question/problem "![](images/4c/4c714262b9da22ea9ad859817db86a3aaf0b29ef811246aedc969bc9999c0348.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0)$, $B(-1,4)$ and $C(3,6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (0) & =1(-3)+3 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (4) & =1(-1)+3 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,6)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (6) & =1(3)+3 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b01faa9-1661-5d2c-8b15-89c1d529166b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498665} {:answer/id #uuid "2773d5bd-6a1e-5e0f-bdc4-1f27d274f0fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498671} {:answer/id #uuid "4546836a-abb8-583d-8041-3599332cf4de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498678} {:answer/id #uuid "86ff2819-d939-51c4-94f3-9732d4521a05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498693} {:answer/id #uuid "961c8a45-200e-5ff7-841b-40c1e1f1d099" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498695}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498693} :answer-field/id #uuid "02799bef-6cfd-5d9e-bca3-3026a3cc6d51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "12a60b9c-85ce-50af-b45d-06caed36a198" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cee718f18c9ef081b3e90a70d4db00ef0339d7d5f0b87423f7c5687709471a6.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-5x-2?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,9),B(-1,4)$ and $C(1,-7).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,9)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (9) & =-5(-2)-2 \\\\ 9 & =8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (4) & =-5(-1)-2 \\\\ 4 & =3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5x-2 \\\\ (-7) & =-5(1)-2 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a90128e-f77f-5ec3-9038-8600c7b3dcfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498681} {:answer/id #uuid "627354bc-e225-5d3c-9eda-85b7e4603569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498682} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0560a4-412e-54e3-91ff-603a3b02dcd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498688} {:answer/id #uuid "8098dcbf-4d2e-5f36-b4e9-f6ca59744fa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498689} {:answer/id #uuid "a27987d5-3a9e-5baf-b1a3-d4be781d9d5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498697}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498681} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed72d909-9af6-5dcf-9647-d3ab941b4b50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "21a9c497-cf26-5338-8f2e-52de8c6489fc" :question/problem "![](images/70/70b04ef6ee89c2bf06db99444f1f89afbe2ea15871f8f79da29668f7be3f9f97.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,-2)$, $B(1,4)$ and $C(2,4).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (-2) & =2(-1)+0 \\\\ -2 & =-2\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(1)+0 \\\\ 4 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,4)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2x \\\\ (4) & =2(2)+0 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498672 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2517ee62-3508-5043-99a6-8cbff4a054bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498670} {:answer/id #uuid "49484dad-6a3e-55b6-a9bc-7f95d103cd98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498679} {:answer/id #uuid "6965c31a-509c-5fad-b07e-299d62f499ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498686} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6fe6ee-5189-5bb5-9dc1-3ca7c751bd17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498696} {:answer/id #uuid "ca1b1055-64cd-5ad9-a4f4-4ba68a08c842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498708}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498686} :answer-field/id #uuid "030b1280-3f72-5e40-9687-4451485960c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498662}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "277a1bc9-d733-576e-9af4-fb70571bb178" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb6b3f51e0e61f72015505469f9fd6e6aa2d5e5b550825e4c761fc78f535ef59.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-7)$, $B(-1,1)$ and $C(1,5).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (-7) & =3(-3)+2 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (1) & =3(-1)+2 \\\\ 1 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,5)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+2 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+2 \\\\ 5 & =5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498698 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b24e4af-347a-5ac2-9514-dd6e178db687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498668} {:answer/id #uuid "70b48381-828b-5d40-b1db-1850c4bb5fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498687} {:answer/id #uuid "aef1cd6c-325f-57b3-b55a-22367510cec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498702} {:answer/id #uuid "b7497970-afdd-59b5-8946-7e774cc44e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498705} {:answer/id #uuid "e81db796-7d07-5404-a2e6-282ce3e715b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498711}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498702} :answer-field/id #uuid "c99296eb-61a0-59b5-b855-4521c40f6736" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498707}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "a390081c-820e-5ce3-b17e-0ab4001a9339" :question/problem "![](images/18/18df2c651366aa361dd4210585c0f9d0607af2f93b6c8b29b14ad1144907fb94.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x-4?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,0),B(-2,-2)$ and $C(2,-8).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (0) & =-2(-3)-4 \\\\ 0 & =2\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (-2) & =-2(-2)-4 \\\\ -2 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x-4 \\\\ (-8) & =-2(2)-4 \\\\ -8 & =-8\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d413d8c-3f61-5d64-83db-8f504335c5bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498673} {:answer/id #uuid "3c85b355-307a-57db-947f-d3ef8d268d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498677} {:answer/id #uuid "83323bd5-5d34-562b-8783-b053fe0eef22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498691} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f856d5-e5e8-54b8-ab43-051a8533362c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498700} {:answer/id #uuid "da7c1cda-1a6a-51a1-bee2-23c37eac0b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498710}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498700} :answer-field/id #uuid "50fbda0d-f2a0-59f8-8288-e3b71a72d78f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498680}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ac37c3c8-b208-5c81-a00d-e1bd9d503cf5" :question/problem "![](images/21/210db4ba3df7f9004c6ffe53336ce3e42d4156841560813478c404353b204c0c.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-4x+1?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,3),B(1,-1)$ and $C(2,-7).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (3) & =-4(0)+1 \\\\ 3 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-1) & =-4(1)+1 \\\\ -1 & =-3\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-7) & =-4(2)+1 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498663} {:answer/id #uuid "0a037906-7560-5a7f-af3a-df39ea31c7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498664} {:answer/id #uuid "2e04fce8-d81f-5c10-9a2d-ce00e7cc6157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498674} {:answer/id #uuid "64c6d466-8db0-5469-a154-b446a630e557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498685} {:answer/id #uuid "cb659afb-f587-5d6a-8397-672e2e9f924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498709}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498663} :answer-field/id #uuid "9124fd28-3c96-58aa-a8b1-46f977a63903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b0bb51db-df3a-5c24-9053-c8f5081141e9" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1aa0849898f763eedd84d050a7bd7c24bbb10c8f89c81e3f533622252330814e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+4.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-5)$, $B(1,5)$ and $C(2,10).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (-5) & =3(-3)+4 \\\\ -5 & =-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+4 \\\\ 5 & =7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,10)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (10) & =3(2)+4 \\\\ 10 & =10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32181eed-9458-5ccf-acc4-92033b733168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498675} {:answer/id #uuid "6485fbd6-7602-59e9-b7db-664adfdbcd5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498684} {:answer/id #uuid "a768ab80-55c6-5d51-80fc-ee9ca1c3c7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498699} {:answer/id #uuid "b31cf4f4-e928-5d0a-810e-cf15a16aed3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498704} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9fccde-11ea-51fa-a5a6-450785e2da15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498713}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498699} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d72100-1cce-5a74-8205-dd9bc89e56ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bbacf92b-66e8-58cd-bc32-e7d565177fbf" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1ff37e7ea63a62de2a1ccbf59c53225b739be305f9e87f7aceca7735ba210bbd.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-3x?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,8),B(0,-2)$ and $C(2,-6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (8) & =-3(-2)+0 \\\\ 8 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (-2) & =-3(0)+0 \\\\ -2 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (-6) & =-3(2)+0 \\\\ -6 & =-6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054694 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054602 :question/id #uuid "6b16ff95-8b78-587d-a7c8-8d0909b69f19" :question/math-academy-id "e-983" :question/problem "Use the table below to plot the graph of $y=3x-2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=3x-2.$\nTherefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=3(0)-2=-2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=3(1)-2=1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=3(2)-2=4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=3(3)-2=7.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $7$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/09/09e670353b2114b229769e2bd6b3eb4a9895389b818fc3f4ace6997a3e7efa3f.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=3x-2.$\n\n![](images/d2/d2d8891102ce99020f544bd8d82a5ff0454080474ce4267ef5285db92f5b2ca0.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2491cf6c-260b-5992-a910-9fe6a80e30bc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048714} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050517}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497787 :question-generator/id #uuid "9ae4d764-bdf7-5b4d-982a-b379ea720263" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186054694.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95871ea8-427c-5d8b-b7b9-90621fa03a1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6a/6a26ee2942f083a2edb99e9839d71577e1772bf6410e1ae4beafcde7f59c7109.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053458} {:answer/id #uuid "c7240b34-1c9b-5ca5-9452-e210e669f37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/893dba533e0afffe05f9603293355ccf38b2723fcd91608ea03fe321e26a0d5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053459} {:answer/id #uuid "17588e8d-da64-5d6b-ab34-45af1c4a7804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/eaf735f72849b82e92f7baf0d991f3e024e013b66d9813d4e0d5f3a87632c901.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053460} {:answer/id #uuid "27023196-b279-5485-8ce7-7bf4dc0c7ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/afb9d602e1bff2fb643f44ed5dfa09d41833740e814739c60d5dd890a2f02270.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053461} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8ce376-c015-5edf-afdd-204f6ccb159f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02f0d3d8bb1bd1e87d05e63579e2a92281de1d000fe2baa7c9942dd80b542efb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053462}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186053459} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bbe1741-021b-5eb6-8d9e-91ce5412b307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4524558d-8a83-5843-a336-69f66463c3a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-54397" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=x-2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=(0)-2=-2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=(1)-2=-1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-2=0,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-2=1.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/4f/4fc0e4386dd956c2b98c844941ce2e27cd1c9ca8578aca4cf5142e6971911831.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=x-2.$\n\n![](images/89/893dba533e0afffe05f9603293355ccf38b2723fcd91608ea03fe321e26a0d5f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8012f237-f895-59fa-8270-6503cec53a98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/33840084a698d261095927ca6ca12e85673665e3dc00264e1d21722a60c16fa4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053812} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce4d676-af93-589c-ba26-6402379e878e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/89/893dba533e0afffe05f9603293355ccf38b2723fcd91608ea03fe321e26a0d5f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053813} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b7f4ba-210d-5ab9-a5f8-a2904e7fedf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/41/416bc4e441bac223991d615915c282fed3ecae8ececd4ce04433a1eacfad47f2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053814} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e4e655-149e-5749-b055-169473ebdae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7e/7e1e94d8d56f09e4c5d2b47cbd04ec99d51f97465d8144683f16a5689fd6324c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053815} {:answer/id #uuid "40c8bec8-cf09-50fd-97ef-11e1dc5e4980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/eaf735f72849b82e92f7baf0d991f3e024e013b66d9813d4e0d5f3a87632c901.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053816}] :answer-field/id #uuid "423e8e65-dd75-5e41-82c6-09a914060bee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186053811}] :question/id #uuid "4cd916a5-f5b2-585b-bea7-8dda3f5e10d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-59676" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y =-x + 1$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186490257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3946c953-9228-5655-b35b-fd707ee85059" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/50/5000be6af7e62672ecacf8fe90aa51286f459dd47f4b44c89c0e5c9fbfff84ac.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489642} {:answer/id #uuid "41956628-242f-5bff-a74b-494fa731d555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/497d1c67fb3a322ae402f6dfa69c8b069d91177ddef6a5847e6dbee4cb93f995.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489664} {:answer/id #uuid "a20e0b6e-d6c8-5746-bf51-509b5c8a9a60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/18/18d9c0adc10639219feaca56d61376d5be64b5b49535c2a92a55f6e5d3422832.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489875} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe1a0f0-9239-5016-8995-7682b6c6771b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/04/0400a1437f26b74feb16161cf51a88c175ee6837fe1e5d8f8785ba2bb2b9c68b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489932} {:answer/id #uuid "d90bc894-c41c-5fae-ad3b-1cd61eefe589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cc/cc985bf7790c1e8b6ec01ecc4b9bcde1c47073591ce02eef867ed652632a819c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489992}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489932} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a58be1d-9b02-526d-a31b-cb5a653e1224" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "60940cd3-550d-521c-8bf6-1906baac5be6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71695" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x+2.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x+2.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)+2=2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)+2=4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)+2=6,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)+2=8.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/6b/6b2da4bfc7c768788d143999fb61e76bb3a60facffc35e430d98085b395932f7.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of  $y=2x+2.$\n\n![](images/04/0400a1437f26b74feb16161cf51a88c175ee6837fe1e5d8f8785ba2bb2b9c68b.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06fa8c2f-5b1f-5063-8e88-0b913061880c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30ea4f86a1a588cd617779bc001935f50b7fa358ecca86efeaf26bde27642627.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497766} {:answer/id #uuid "09af78ca-b5c2-58ed-aee4-4ddfc7a7f013" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f3/f3b91b84281ef5b4936438c7e92935cbaf15d17ee50b33a27a7bed638391ef74.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497767} {:answer/id #uuid "29968d51-b8a6-5bee-82fc-d738be24cc8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b9/b9758c660c06a62ba10ca7ced102655a3a8f376d31d9c4ef73ec9ea8b33e769b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497770} {:answer/id #uuid "7083980a-a87f-5d35-b45a-36f6cd7e349b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/07b33747d01621cb73ae464999a8d6a135f0dc579f9e50b250f34b3df9ca4783.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497779} {:answer/id #uuid "f90d513b-aef2-5217-be5f-bd7b7f1eafff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497786}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497786} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad570f02-ebbc-528a-ba9a-40d1735ee18e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5a903cf9-42ce-5563-9b36-303a8f1c1320" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x-3.$.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x-3.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=-(0)-3=-3,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=-(1)-3=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-(2)-3=-5,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)-3=-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $-6$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/c9/c96b7da7b073986de68a557df8a9dbde16d39566c87eb0b5ba6ac62bd40da7c4.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x-3.$\n\n![](images/05/05d10ee3d2e6bc295a7d2e6b07ca726c9c11c159d74f1d81c71fce761fa4275e.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "505696e7-5c70-5bfb-9d5d-53a811375cd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e6/e65396cb057b7306ae81557f25d24f797e736ad37c09ddb0e67ee19c4e9ab318.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497773} {:answer/id #uuid "685c2324-6319-5bc5-b432-4f7efc03eacb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/db/dbddb21434456cdcb99c4ba0660c65615c97538ccbdcf2d6057e855d0d30f8f9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497778} {:answer/id #uuid "816e9948-7eb3-5b5d-9fb6-b4ad3fb7ff4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4bb98a9deb3f1049e3b2eeffca7deccfefb79fd5d893b89940be52fbce397d8a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497780} {:answer/id #uuid "8497b882-b57f-5efb-b03e-5229284a8b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497781} {:answer/id #uuid "e100f2db-5cdc-57b9-ba80-cfeb83c61519" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/54c37e2aadc0f1a3db8ec1f39905b1e694804df7680999079f1d2a2017c09794.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497785}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497781} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f305ae-b441-5bc6-833a-ae8108df72ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497771}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5da1545d-7bf4-538f-94f3-464d21187a82" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x-6.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)-6=-4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)-6=-2,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)-6=0.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/95/958c5a848a09e43832324b8afb000348c7630cd2c42e99a51215d48d9895a00e.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of  $y=2x-6.$\n\n![](images/3e/3efb14f33400cd4a6353b93e5d99a826083cca6859785d5bd5d837fb00ad302f.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b68311-0695-52e7-984f-b1f413574531" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f59cdf977a5aa60bea4bbe522a20e29c3d13caa13ce178b5038569da0282bf04.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497768} {:answer/id #uuid "10291a72-b265-5a7e-ae36-03727e2c077a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d8/d89b7a9495d61d6c67332c05aa99d35957782b600b447bb0a70dbf3595857f83.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497769} {:answer/id #uuid "3cb40a26-7dd0-53a3-8f8b-50d6ae6b03aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497772} {:answer/id #uuid "c411d8f7-79b2-5537-91be-c623daad8c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/15/15bdb2e49885cb6bc9ea7aeccff0cb3227504f5b122f0f16e51bc2e6154d01c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497783} {:answer/id #uuid "dcebd751-9faf-5113-a03b-26d02cbb100e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c6/c62998935843f79fcf2007edbfe243071b75c9ceb63babf46cad3c6aa507291c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497784}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497772} :answer-field/id #uuid "645e1d5a-90c9-50c4-b1ae-f7aff3a3dba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "67365bc6-453f-5a19-82a4-9817c6e05a99" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-6.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=(1)-6=-5,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-6=-4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-6=-3.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/99/99188f2a0f8de0054a6375a88a11242bea7e4799cc17552cd9ba0dd00d5a0788.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n![](images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Plotting a Line Using a Table"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054695 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054603 :question/id #uuid "4aad1578-4134-5f25-88cb-8ab4631257ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-984" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\nIt is often easiest to pick one of the points to have an $x$-coordinate of $x=0.$ So, for the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(0)+3 \\\\  & =0+3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,3).$\n\nFor the second point, let's choose $x=4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(4)+3 \\\\  & =-2+3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(4,1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3.$\n\n![](images/36/36689081acaacb24a09826c3927388697e77d92caeca900d053d33d0f99d2b8c.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebeb4e5a-adbe-5a94-b05d-61933a687892" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497765 :question-generator/id #uuid "5acf3299-1ee4-5045-8a1b-4834747495c0" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186054695.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/